v3.0 AmiNet ANSI-Colored Text File Listings.

Suitable for use on ANY Amiga BBS program, in your readable text file area. This archive includes numerous subdirectories of listings found on the following AmiNet CD-Roms: 5, 6, Set I, 7, 8, Set II, 9, and 10. 

Each subdirectory houses listings for each sub-area of a larger area on AmiNet. For instance, there's a "Biz/" subdirectory which houses individual listings for: database files, demo files, dopus files, miscelaneous files, and patches.

Each listing is fully colorized using ANSI color codes, so should be presented to your users very nicely. Each listing also includes a neat Ascii Title screen you may wish to use as an entry screen for each area.

Lastly, the "CD Location" column was cleaned up a bit, so as to be a bit easier to understand for your users. Files located in Set 1 are notated using the characters 1A, 1B, 1C, and 1D, whereas files on Set II use 2a, 2b, 2c, and 2d respectively. I also replaced the "space" with "10", so users will know which files are located on the(what was current) CD # 10.

Finally, installation instructions for BOTH CNet 3.xx and v4.xx, as well as specific instructions for SysOps using something OTHER than CNet Amiga are also included.

In short, ENJOY these files! :-)

Dotoran/Dave Weeks

